-- title:
--   Multidegree map modulo dual-graph Laplacians for semistable coverings
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $\pi \in A$ a nonzero element of the maximal ideal of $A$; let $F$ be a field extension of $L$. Fix $n, m \in \mathbb{N}$ and, for each $i < n$, a field $\bar F_i$ over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ satisfying `HasPrincipalDivisors` (each nonzero element has a finitely supported divisor computing its orders at all places, of degree $0$) and with all places of $\bar F_i$ rational over $\kappa$ (the structure map onto the residue field of the place being surjective), together with a `ComponentChart` $C_i$ of $F$ over $A$ with residue field $\bar F_i$, all places of $F$ in $(C_i).\mathrm{dom}$ being rational over $L$. Fix annuli $\mathrm{An}_e, \mathrm{An}'_e$ ($e < m$), indices $\mathrm{src}_e, \mathrm{tgt}_e < n$, places $x^{s}_e$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{src}_e}$ and $x^{t}_e$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{tgt}_e}$, and weights $w_e \in \mathbb{N}$ such that: $\mathrm{An}'_e$ and $\mathrm{An}_e$ have the same domain and the same modulus, that modulus is nonzero in $L$ and equals a unit of $A$ times $\pi^{w_e}$, and the two parameters multiply to the image of the modulus; $\mathrm{An}_e$ is attached to $C_{\mathrm{src}_e}$ at $x^{s}_e$ and $\mathrm{An}'_e$ to $C_{\mathrm{tgt}_e}$ at $x^{t}_e$ in the sense of `IsAttached` (the place is a node of the chart, the annulus parameter lies in the chart's integers with residue of order $1$ at that place, and the unit-slope condition holds for every element of the chart's integers with nonzero residue and vanishing order along the annulus); every node $x$ of every $C_i$ is an end $(\mathrm{src}_e, x^{s}_e)$ or $(\mathrm{tgt}_e, x^{t}_e)$ of some annulus, and no point $(i,x)$ with $x$ a node of $C_i$ is an end in two ways (uniqueness over $\mathrm{Fin}\,m \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,m$); and every place of $F$ over $L$ lies either in exactly one chart domain and in no annulus domain, or in exactly one annulus domain and in no chart domain. Let $V$ be the disjoint union of $\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ with the sets of $w_e - 1$ interior indices of the annuli, let the edges be the pairs $(e,k)$ with $k < w_e$, with ends $\mathrm{src}_e$ for $k = 0$ and the interior vertex $(e,k-1)$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{tgt}_e$ for $k+1 = w_e$ and the interior vertex $(e,k)$ otherwise, and let $\mathrm{lap} : V \to (V \to \mathbb{Z})$ be the associated graph Laplacian. The conclusion asserts the existence of an additive homomorphism $\varphi$ from the divisors $\mathrm{Place}\,L\,F \to_{0} \mathbb{Z}$ of $F/L$ to $(V \to \mathbb{Z})$ modulo the subgroup generated by the range of $\mathrm{lap}$ such that: a place in $(C_i).\mathrm{dom}$ is sent to the class of the basis vector of the vertex $i$; a place $P$ in $(\mathrm{An}_e).\mathrm{dom}$ at which the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the annulus parameter lies in $A$ and equals a unit times $\pi^d$ with $0 < d < w_e$ is sent to the class of the basis vector of the interior vertex $(e, d-1)$; a place in $(\mathrm{An}_e).\mathrm{dom}$ whose parameter value is not of the form (unit)$\cdot\pi^d$ in $A$ is sent to $0$; and $\varphi D = 0$ whenever $f \in F$ is nonzero, $D$ computes the orders $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ at all places, and every place in the support of $D$ lies in some chart domain or in some annulus domain with parameter value of the shape (unit)$\cdot\pi^d$ in $A$.
--
--   This is the specialisation, or multidegree, map attaching to a divisor on $F/L$ its position on the dual graph of the given semistable covering by component charts and annuli, taken modulo Laplacians, i.e. valued in the divisor class group of that graph; principal divisors supported on the charts and on the integral points of the annuli are killed. It is the combinatorial input to the subsequent bounds on the torsion of the tropical position and on the component group of a semistable model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_multidegree_of_semistableCovering.lean

